phase-084: a narrow deny is not a deny

The dispatcher resolved `agent.reviewer.permission.<key>` with the same rule
the project's suite used: a bare action, or an object of pattern -> action
whose patterns all carry the same action. opencode does not read it that way.
It evaluates the LAST matching rule, so {"*.md": "deny"} denies the markdown
files and leaves every other path to the rules above it - and the global
config grants "external_directory": {"**": "allow"} above the agent's own
rules. A reviewer that could read outside the checkout would have started
the review.

The guard now refuses a narrow deny, and says which key and why. The
request's "with these keys denied:" line no longer counts one as denied.
The pipeline's own smoke suite asserts it: a narrow-pattern deny stops the
review, and the refusal names the key.

232 checks, green (230 before).
